Note: Remit Type (Check/Wire) on Manual TAR jobs — Edit & Balance Details page

The "Select Remit Type" dropdown always has both Check and Wire options in it. For Manual TAR jobs, the dropdown will always appear greyed out / locked on "Check" — this is expected behavior today, not a bug in the current story.
Reason: whether the dropdown can be changed at all depends on a flag tied to the agency (whether the agency is set up for wire payments). For every Manual TAR job, that flag is currently always "No" — it's never set to "Yes" for Manual jobs, only for regular (Mass) jobs.
Because of that, Manual jobs can never be switched to Wire today. This isn't caused by anything being fixed/changed in this story (US-132325) — it comes from the separate process that creates Manual TAR jobs in the first place, which never sets up the wire flag.
What to test: Confirm the dropdown is locked/disabled and shows "Check" for Manual jobs — that is the correct, expected result. It should not be logged as a defect under this story. If Wire support for Manual jobs is needed, it should be raised as a separate item against the Manual TAR job-creation process, not against this story's changes.


