DECLARE @RunName VARCHAR(10) = 'MN262008';   -- <-- set RunName
DECLARE @RunDate DATE       = '2026-09-21'; -- <-- set RunDate (date only is fine)

SELECT
    s.CustID,
    s.RunName,
    s.RunDate,
    s.AgencyID,
    s.RunType,
    s.RemitType                    AS Summary_RemitType,
    m.SpecialInstrInd               AS ManualHeader_SpecialInstrInd,
    m.RemitType                     AS ManualHeader_RemitType
FROM Lat_TaxAmount_Summary (NOLOCK) s
LEFT JOIN lat_Manual_TAR_Reports_384 (NOLOCK) m
       ON m.RunName     = s.RunName
      AND m.CustomerID  = s.CustID
      AND m.AgencyID    = s.AgencyID
      AND CAST(m.RunDate AS DATE) = CAST(s.RunDate AS DATE)
WHERE s.RunName = @RunName
  AND CAST(s.RunDate AS DATE) = @RunDate;


How to read the result:

ManualHeader_SpecialInstrInd = 'Y' → the Remit Type dropdown will be enabled/editable for that agency on that job.
ManualHeader_SpecialInstrInd = 'N' (or no matching row) → the dropdown will be locked on Check.
Summary_RemitType / ManualHeader_RemitType show what's actually saved — for Manual jobs today, expect 'Check' (or blank), never 'Wire'.